cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Reader's Book of Mormon: A Colometric Edition"
authors:
  - name: "Stan the Bible Man"
    email: "thebibleman77@gmail.com"
date-released: "2026-05-10"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bibleman-stan/readers-bofm"
url: "https://bomreader.com"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A colometric reading edition of the Book of Mormon (2020 LDS text)
  designed for ESL readers, students, and newcomers. Each line on the
  page renders one atomic thought unit (ATU). The edition is produced
  via the ATU apparatus (atu-method) — a proposition-first generative
  framework with structural justifications, merge-overrides, and
  Universal-Dependencies-driven mechanical validation. Includes
  optional archaic-word modernization layer, audio narration, and
  per-chapter study overlays.
keywords:
  - Book of Mormon
  - colometric edition
  - reading edition
  - atomic thought unit
  - ATU
  - sense-lines
  - scripture
references:
  - type: software
    title: "ATU Method: Computational Colometry for Canonical Texts"
    authors:
      - name: "Stan the Bible Man"
        email: "thebibleman77@gmail.com"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/bibleman-stan/atu-method"
    notes: "Methodology and apparatus used to produce this edition."
